<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original GirlfriendGPT comparisons, primary sources, updates, adult boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Every page must answer a real reader question. Keywords belong in clear titles, headings, direct answers, and natural explanations—not repetition or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link to official pages where possible. Privacy and security guidance relies on recognized primary resources. We identify uncertainty and require live verification for changing plans and features.</p><h2>Adult boundaries</h2><p>Coverage concerns adults and emphasizes consenting fictional scenarios, privacy, cost visibility, and emotional boundaries. We never request private chats, credentials, or intimate personal images.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Requests should identify the URL, disputed statement, and a direct source supporting the correction.</p></InfoPage>
